  "body": "Hello lovely humans,\n\n[webpack-dev-server](https://www.npmjs.com/package/webpack-dev-server) just published its new version 1.15.0.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      State\n    </th>\n    <td>\n      Failing tests :rotating_light:\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Dependency\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      webpack-dev-server\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      New version\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      1.15.0\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Type\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      devDependency\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nThis version is **covered** by your **current version range** and after updating it in your project **the build went from success to failure**.\n\nAs webpack-dev-server is “only” a devDependency of this project it **might not break production or downstream projects**, but “only” your build or test tools – **preventing new deploys or publishes**.\n\nI recommend you give this issue a high priority. I’m sure you can resolve this :muscle:\n\nOf course this could just be a false positive, caused by a flaky test suite, or third parties that are currently broken or unavailable, but that would be another problem I’d recommend working on.\n\nDo you have any ideas how I could improve these pull requests? Did I report anything you think isn’t right?\nAre you unsure about how things are supposed to work?\n\nThere is a collection of [frequently asked questions](https://greenkeeper.io/faq.html) and while I’m just a bot, there is a group of people who are happy to teach me new things. [Let them know](https://github.com/greenkeeperio/greenkeeper/issues/new).\n\nGood luck with your project :sparkles:\n\nYou rock!\n\n:palm_tree:\n\n---\n\nThe new version differs by 39 commits .\n- [`f1ce64f`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/f1ce64f848bf5165b457fbdfff4cc5432b1f313a) <code>1.15.0</code>\n- [`cdbda1d`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/cdbda1d38b7c803ac856fd4e36f2d83a2da004b9) <code>Add changelog</code>\n- [`838b58a`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/838b58af0b22303693d11becbaa807f7a771c702) <code>Enable linting for some forgotten files</code>\n- [`9973128`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/99731281ce06dac367a61334e265e15bf1fbf9d6) <code>pass this to setup. Fixes #536</code>\n- [`38624be`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/38624beec4e4aefd5c1b1ece799c9fa38554694c) <code>Assigned --cacert CLI argument to correct options property</code>\n- [`31b0a1a`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/31b0a1a9cb00b33d4050ea764a40e538a547a23b) <code>set headers on all requests to support e.g. CORS</code>\n- [`4713e97`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/4713e970ec76a3bd3bbb96e41015099b20af7c41) <code>update dependencies</code>\n- [`47c1699`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/47c169972f5dbbeac172018447292640888ef461) <code>merged #443</code>\n- [`8da1e57`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/8da1e57ca0a552076b8ad87fb7135379d95b91a6) <code>FIX console.log spacing</code>\n- [`daa1baf`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/daa1baf340ec94baa727c2d24e50462d3294b9e6) <code>Don't reload app upon proxy errors.</code>\n- [`31f6ac1`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/31f6ac125df89a2de83a2f6f576b70fc37b2e41b) <code>Allow running dev-server behind https proxy</code>\n- [`f28944e`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/f28944e1dc84a832215cda3fcd87178a068c8b99) <code>Update self signed ssl certificates</code>\n- [`3767f41`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/3767f4149bce129f2d39dd4e3842eaf7838d6388) <code>Allow to use port from current page, the same way we allow to use hostname.</code>\n- [`0f013aa`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/0f013aa74e969385c58d0a90fcae01eda54d2c7e) <code>correct proxy options</code>\n- [`1c04206`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/commit/1c0420636a1a6580f146476f1c76eda27f4c512a) <code>add `staticOptions` for expose express.static options pass in</code>\n\nThere are 39 commits in total. See the [full diff](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-dev-server/compare/eae3a0c73fb847521b42ac2accae1c0906dd6023...f1ce64f848bf5165b457fbdfff4cc5432b1f313a).\n\n---\n\nThis pull request was created by [greenkeeper.io](https://greenkeeper.io/).\n\n<sub>Tired of seeing this sponsor message? :zap: `greenkeeper upgrade`</sub>\n",
